{ [Last Modified: 7/10/2020]
[ This study is in progress.]
This study was cloned by hand from
https://lichess.org/study/Uw4P5qvl
See that study first.

This study is part of my Advanced Course. The idea of the study is to do deliberate practice on annotating your games and doing chess research. Annotating your own games is one of the best ways to improve your chess. Doing that with the aid of a strong player is best. The chess research you do will depend on your games and your interest. Get help from your mentor on how to do the research.

The studies are graduated difficulty. The first studies could be done by advanced beginners.

It takes time to do quality deliberate practice annotating your games. Expect to take a few hours for each!

This study is linked from
Advanced: Curriculum: Annotating Games
https://lichess.org/study/VHcKZ37M/Iv8iaoku
- }
