{ [HTWCGQ pg 18]
-
This game opens with the Ruy Lopez Morphy defense. White tries to bust the center open immediately with 5.d4. Black attempts to counter this with an unsound attacking move (6...Nxd4). White then essays a questionable gambit, which Black accepts. On the very next move Black errors, and White presses the attack to victory.
- }
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. d4 { Premature, but playable. } 5... b5 { Better is ...exd4 as in the following line. } (5... exd4 6. O-O Be7 { The solid choice. } 7. e5 Ne4 8. Nxd4 O-O 9. Nf5 d5 { As usual in the King pawn games, if Black can play ...d5, he gets equality. }) 6. Bb3 Nxd4? { This is a tactical error. } 7. Bxf7+!? { White plays a questionable gambit here. Simple and good was 7.Nxd4 as in the next line. } (7. Nxd4 c5 8. Nf5 c4 9. Nd6+ Bxd6 10. Qxd6 cxb3 11. Qxe5+ Qe7 12. Qxe7+ Kxe7 13. axb3 Nxe4 $16 { White is better because Black will take a few moves to "castle by hand", and will lose more time once the Knight is kicked off e4 and tries to find a good home. }) 7... Kxf7 8. Nxe5+ Ke6? { Moving into the center of the board is an error. Better was ...Kg8. See the next line. } (8... Kg8 9. Qxd4 c5 10. Qe3? { A natural mistake. } 10... Bb7 { Black will play ...Qc7, ...d5. White does not have enough pieces mobilized to take advantage of Black's King position. }) 9. Qxd4 { Whites threats areare 9.Nf3, 9.Nc3, 9.Bg5. Black is in trouble. } 9... c5 10. Qc3 Nxe4 11. Qe3 { White offers the Knight. } 11... Kxe5?? { Black blunders by bringing his King even further up the board into White's territory. 11...Qg5 was better. } (11... Qg5 12. f4 Qxg2 13. Rg1 Qxc2 14. Na3 Qxh2 15. Nf3 Qf2+ 16. Qxf2 Nxf2 17. Kxf2 $16) 12. Nc3 d5 13. Nxe4 d4 { Instead ...Kf5, but Black is lost whatever he plays. } (13... dxe4 14. Qf4+ Ke6 15. Qxe4+ Kf7 16. Qxa8 $18 { Winning. }) 14. Qf3 Bd7 15. O-O Be7 16. Re1 { Black resigned.
White's entire army is read to come out swinging. Black's King cannot survive in the center of the board.
Stockfish says mate in 8. For example... } 16... Bf5 17. Bf4+ Ke6 18. Nd6+ Kd7 19. Qb7+ Qc7 20. Rxe7+ Kxe7 21. Qxc7+ Bd7 22. Re1+ Kf8 23. Qxd7 c4 24. Qf7# 1-0


